				"uid" : {
					"__type" : "uid",
					"uidString" : "SvJtZY7YT6Sy1LCWa/eESQ=="
				},
				"paragraphStyle" : {
					"__type" : "textStyle"
				},
				"string" : "Carp secretly has two languages in one file: the one that becomes a program, and the one that runs inside the compiler while it decides what that program will be. Macros belong to the second, and if you’ve ever written one, you know how hard they are to follow when all you see is what went in and what came out."
			},
			{
				"__type" : "textSnippet",
				"children" : {
					"__type" : "snippets",
					"items" : [ ]
				},
				"createEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"createTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-09-26T21:49:16.267433+02:00"
					}
				},
				"editEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"editTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-09-26T21:49:16.267433+02:00"
					}
				},
				"uid" : {
					"__type" : "uid",
					"uidString" : "MoBrtzroTL2aZSl4oyfTFQ=="
				},
				"paragraphStyle" : {
					"__type" : "textStyle"
				},
				"string" : "So let’s look at what happens in between! The Expand action on a Carp snippet opens a {{gtClass:CarpMacroExpansion}}: the form as written, and every expansion step taken from it. We can step forward, step back, or expand fully to see what the compiler will actually compile. And we can do so without fear, since expansion runs against a private copy of the compile-time environment and never touches the session."
			},
			{
				"__type" : "textSnippet",
				"children" : {
					"__type" : "snippets",
					"items" : [ ]
				},
				"createEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"createTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-09-26T21:49:16.267433+02:00"
					}
				},
				"editEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"editTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-09-26T21:49:16.267433+02:00"
					}
				},
				"uid" : {
					"__type" : "uid",
					"uidString" : "dgWyQWPQRrSo9WaRVc9Mug=="
				},
				"paragraphStyle" : {
					"__type" : "textStyle"
				},
				"string" : "A step is one reduction anywhere in the form, outermost first, then each subform in order. Here is what that looks like, and this one even works without a server:"
			},
			{
				"__type" : "textSnippet",
				"children" : {
